This capture shows this device performing DNS lookups for multiple cloud services (Microsoft, Bing, Sentry.io, Azure PrivateLink). DNS is the first step in almost every HTTPS transaction, and these queries reveal what services your system is trying to communicate with. This is normal background traffic for Windows, Edge, and cloud connected applications.
This capture shows DNS resolution activity from a local device (10.218.252.191) to a DNS server (10.218.252.84). The device is resolving several cloud service domains, including Bing, Microsoft Graph, Sentry.io, and Azure PrivateLink identity endpoints. These domains are commonly used for cloud APIs, browser telemetry, and application error reporting. The presence of both DNS queries and responses indicates normal background communication as applications establish secure HTTPS connections. This capture demonstrates the first stage of an HTTP/HTTPS transaction: DNS resolution. 
What this capture shows (interpreting the packets)
✔ 1. The device is resolving multiple domains
