✔ 3. It captured both DNS queries and DNS responses
This is important because:
•	Queries show what your device wants to talk to
•	Responses show what IP addresses those domains resolve to
This is the foundation of SOC investigation.
✔ 4. This is normal background traffic
Nothing here is malicious.
But learning to interpret this traffic is essential because:
•	Malware also uses DNS
•	DNS tunneling is used for exfiltration
•	Suspicious domains often appear first in DNS
•	IoT devices reveal their behavior through DNS
This is why DNS analysis is one of the first skills SOC analysts learn.
