✔ DNS is the first indicator of compromise
Malware often reveals itself through:
•	Strange domains
•	Domain generation algorithms (DGA)
•	High frequency queries
•	Rare TLDs
•	Failed lookups
This capture shows normal traffic — but now we know what normal looks like.
✔ DNS is how to detect IoT misbehavior
In this Home SOC + OT/ICS Lab:
•	Cameras
•	Smart switches
•	Thermostats
•	IoT devices
…all generate DNS traffic.
If an IoT device starts querying:
•	Unknown servers
•	Foreign domains
•	High frequency patterns
That’s a red flag.
✔ DNS is how you detect exfiltration
Attackers often use:
•	DNS tunneling
•	TXT record abuse
•	Long subdomains
•	Encoded payloads
Your capture is clean — but this is the foundation.

